#Noebbly-prep.lic
#Paladin version of Brayis-prep.lic (Noebbly) -- sword and shield, no rubs (he has no
#rub items), so gearing up for combat is clearing hands and readying the weapon and
#the shield. STORE LIST (11/03): weapon = the falchion (put in sheath), shield = the
#greatshield (worn if possible, stowed otherwise), so STORE/READY WEAPON and SHIELD
#do the right thing.
#
#The spell prep the profiles used to list (prep 1604, evoke ..., gird) is NOT here:
#leave it after "script Noebbly-prep" in hunting_prep_commands.

module NoebblyPrep

# clear hands -- "store weapon" routes the falchion to the sheath, "store shield"
# wears the shield again; "stow all" mops up anything left in a hand.
fput "store weapon"
fput "store shield"
fput "stow all"

fput "ready weapon"
fput "ready shield"

# Nothing in the weapon hand: the weapon is really gone (disarmed and never
# recovered, or the STORE weapon setting points at something that isn't there).
# Don't let bigshot walk back out unarmed -- stop it here, in town, the same way
# Brayis-prep.lic does.
pause 0.5
if checkright.nil?
  echo "Noebbly-prep: nothing in the right hand after READY WEAPON -- stopping bigshot. " \
       "Check the STORE weapon setting (STORE LIST)."
  Script.kill("bigshot") if Script.running?("bigshot")
  exit
end

# Puts away loot eloot has no room for and unpauses it, so a full cloak can't
# leave you fighting with your hands full (see eloot_guard.lic).
Script.start("eloot_guard") unless Script.running?("eloot_guard")

# Rescue-child bounty: when the child finds you mid-hunt, stop and run echild right there
# instead of hunting on with her in tow (two children died that way 11/07; see child_watch.lic;
# ;vars set child_rescue=off to disable).
Script.start("child_watch") unless Script.running?("child_watch")

end #End of module
